Original commit body from 6e5c6dc:

Three UX improvements when using -x/--exclude-tests:

1. Remove misleading "Coverage requires execution" message
   - When coverage cannot be estimated (no production functions),
     simply omit the coverage line instead of showing a confusing hint
   - Removed unused COVERAGE_HINTS dict and _get_coverage_hint function

2. Overview totals now match -x semantics
   - Shows "2 files (2 non-test + 0 test)" instead of "6 files (2 + 4)"
   - Total equals non-test count when excluding tests
   - Makes clear that tests are truly being ignored in the counts

3. Structure section filters test files in directory counts
   - Tests directory now shows count of non-test items only
   - Config/doc files (Makefile, Cargo.toml) still counted
   - Test source files and test subdirectories excluded from count
